1.text:
The five exemplars are all C V C and the final consonant is always taken
from the set

      { d , b , t , w }

dad – d , dab – b , gut – t , low – w , cat – t .

The five negative exemplars all break that final-letter condition

ear – r , cop – p , ego – o , mom – m , ate – e .

Hence, up to the usual C V C framing, a word is in the family iff its third
letter is d / b / t / w.

On the five candidates

* leg – l e g  third = g ∉ {d,b,t,w}
* dam – d a m  third = m ∉ {d,b,t,w}
* rat – r a t  third = t ∈ {d,b,t,w}
* car – c a r  third = r ∉ {d,b,t,w}
* bin – b i n  third = n ∉ {d,b,t,w}

is the only one that satisfies the final-letter condition, i.e. it is the
only one that is in the same family as dad dab gut low cat.  In particular
leg, dam, car and bin are all ordinary non-members of the family; e.g.
leg is a clear non-member.  If a single “odd-one-out’’ among the five
alternatives is wanted, rat is the unique member of the family and the
other four, leg/dam/car/bin, are the non-members.

