5.text:
The five positives are all CVC and the third consonant is always drawn from the
same closed set.

dad = d a d   third = d
dab = d a b   third = b
gut = g u t   third = t
low = l o w   third = w
cat = c a t   third = t

so

* C V C
* V ∈ {a,o,u}
* third ∈ {b,d,t,w}

is sufficient to separate the exemplars from the declared negatives

ear third = r ∉ {b,d,t,w}
cop third = p ∉ {b,d,t,w}
ego  V C V
mom third = m ∉ {b,d,t,w}
ate  V C V and third = e ∉ {b,d,t,w}

On the five test items

leg = l e g   C V C, V = e ∉ {a,o,u}, third = g ∉ {b,d,t,w}
dam = d a m   C V C, V = a ok, third = m ∉ {b,d,t,w}
rat = r a t   C V C, V = a ok, third = t ∈ {b,d,t,w}
car = c a r   C V C, V = a ok, third = r ∉ {b,d,t,w}
bin = b i n   C V C, V = i ∉ {a,o,u}, third = n ∉ {b,d,t,w}

rat is the only item of the five that keeps the C V C / third-letter {b,d,t,w}
description, i.e. it is the only one that belongs to the dad/dab/gut/low/cat
family.  Hence A, B, D and E are all ordinary non-members of the family.

If a single canonical non-member has to be named the textbook case is

A. leg = l e g

it violates the vowel condition V ∈ {a,o,u} and the third-letter condition
third ∈ {b,d,t,w} at once, and it is the clearest illustration that the
family does not admit e-vowels and a final g.  dam, car and bin are non-members
for the same final-letter reason, with rat being the unique member of the
family among the options.

1.text:
The five positives are all C V C and the final consonant is the cue.

* dad = d a d   3rd = d
* dab = d a b   3rd = b
* gut = g u t   3rd = t
* low = l o w   3rd = w
* cat = c a t   3rd = t

so the family is C V C with V ∈ {a,o,u} and 3rd ∈ {d,b,t,w}. 
That is exactly what rules the five negatives out

* ear = e a r   3rd = r ∉ {d,b,t,w}
* cop = c o p   3rd = p ∉ {d,b,t,w}
* ego = e g o   not C V C and 3rd = o ∉ {d,b,t,w}
* mom = m o m   3rd = m ∉ {d,b,t,w}
* ate = a t e   not C V C and 3rd = e ∉ {d,b,t,w}

On the five test items

* leg = l e g   C V C but V = e ∉ {a,o,u} and 3rd = g ∉ {d,b,t,w}
* dam = d a m   C V C, V = a ok, 3rd = m ∉ {d,b,t,w}
* rat = r a t   C V C, V = a ok, 3rd = t ∈ {d,b,t,w}
* car = c a r   C V C, V = a ok, 3rd = r ∉ {d,b,t,w}
* bin = b i n   C V C but V = i ∉ {a,o,u} and 3rd = n ∉ {d,b,t,w}

Hence up to the final-letter / C V C description rat is the only
choice that belongs to the dad/dab/gut/low/cat class.  The other four
choices are ordinary non-members of the family.  Leg is a textbook
non-member: it contains the forbidden vowel e and its third letter g
is not in {d,b,t,w}, e.g. A. leg is a clear word that does not follow
the pattern, the same being true of B dam, D car and E bin.

